{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":61377481,"ns":0,"title":"Heterodactylus lundii","revisions":[{"revid":1355140902,"parentid":1283044345,"minor":true,"timestamp":"2026-05-20T03:43:41Z","size":3370,"sha1":"7416547c2d7c7b830c5da73f6fc448ae8e683a06","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{short description|Species of lizard}}\n{{speciesbox\n| image = \n| status = EN\n| status_system = IUCN3.1\n| status_ref = <ref name=iucn>[[species:Adriano Lima Silveira|Silveira AL]] et al. (20 authors) (2021). \"''Heterodactylus lundii'' \". The [[IUCN]] Red List of Threatened Species 2021: https://dx.doi.org/10.2305/IUCN.UK.2021-3.RLTS.T134884763A134884765.pt. Accessed on 29 March 2025. (in English and Portuguese).</ref>\n| genus = Heterodactylus\n| species = lundii\n| authority = [[Johannes Theodor Reinhardt|Reinhardt]] & [[Christian Frederik Lütken|Lütken]], 1862\n| synonyms = \n}}\n\n'''''Heterodactylus lundii''''', also known [[Common name|commonly]] as '''Lund's teiid''', is an [[Endangered species|endangered]] [[species]] of [[lizard]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Gymnophthalmidae]].<ref name=RDB>{{NRDB species |genus=Heterodactylus |species=lundii |accessdate=27 July 2019}}</ref> The species is [[Endemism|endemic]] to [[Brazil]].\n\n==Etymology==\nThe [[Specific name (zoology)|specific name]], ''lundii'', is in honor of Danish [[Paleontology|paleontologist]] [[Peter Wilhelm Lund]].<ref>[[Bo Beolens|Beolens, Bo]]; [[Michael Watkins (zoologist)|Watkins, Michael]]; [[Michael Grayson|Grayson, Michael]] (2011). ''The Eponym Dictionary of Reptiles''. Baltimore: Johns Hopkins University Press. xiii + 296 pp. {{ISBN|978-1-4214-0135-5}}. (''Heterodactylus lundii'', pp. 162–163).</ref>\n\n==Description==\n''Heterodactylus lundii'' has an elongated body and very small legs. It may attain a [[Snout–vent length|snout-to-vent length]] (SVL) of {{cvt|6|cm|in}}. The tail length is about twice the SVL.<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==Geographic range==\n''Heterodactylus lundii'' is found in the Brazilian state of [[Minas Gerais]].<ref name=iucn/><ref name=RDB/>\n\n==Habitat==\nThe preferred natural [[habitat]] of ''Heterodactylus lundii'' is [[savanna]], at altitudes of {{cvt|900|–|1,300|m|ft}}.<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==Behavior==\n''Heterodactylus lundii'' is [[Terrestrial locomotion|terrestrial]] and [[fossorial]].<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==Reproduction==\n''Heterodactylus lundii'' is [[Oviparity|oviparous]].<ref name=iucn/><ref name=RDB/> [[Clutch (eggs)|Clutch]] size is only two eggs.<ref name=iucn/>\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n==Further reading==\n*[[George Albert Boulenger|Boulenger GA]] (1885). ''Catalogue of the Lizards in The British Museum (Natural History). Second Edition. Volume II. ... Teiidæ'' ...'''.''' London: Trustees of the British Museum (Natural History). (Taylor and Francis, printers). xiii + 497 + Plates I–XXIV. (''Heterodactylus lundii'', p. 423).\n*{{cite journal |last1=Reinhardt |first1=J. |author1-link=Johannes Theodor Reinhardt |last2=Lütken |first2=C. |author2-link=Christian Frederik Lütken |title=''Bidrag til Kundskab om Brasiliens Padder og Krybdyr '' |journal=Videnskabelige Meddelelser fra den naturhistoriske Forening i Kjöbenhavn |date=1862 |volume=1861 |issue=10–15 |pages=143–242}} + Plates I–VI. (''Heterodactylus lundii'', new species, pp. 214–218 + Plate VI, figures 10, 10a–10f). (in Danish).\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q5258372}}\n\n[[Category:Heterodactylus]]\n[[Category:Spectacled lizards of Brazil]]\n[[Category:Endemic reptiles of Brazil]]\n[[Category:Reptiles described in 1862]]\n[[Category:Taxa named by Johannes Theodor Reinhardt]]\n[[Category:Taxa named by Christian Frederik Lütken]]\n\n{{Gymnophthalmidae-stub}}"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-10-30T06:17:16Z","lastrevid":1355140902,"length":3370}]}}